s","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/deployments","created_at":"2021-12-14T20:05:30Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T23:41:45Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-04T23:46:17Z","git_url":"git://github.com/honojs/hono.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:honojs/hono.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono","homepage":"https://hono.dev","size":9897,"stargazers_count":32411,"watchers_count":32411,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1372,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":415,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["aws-lambda","bun","cloudflare","cloudflare-workers","deno","npm","router","typescript","web-framework"],"visibility":"public","forks":1372,"open_issues":415,"watchers":32411,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/5384","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5384","diff_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5384.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5384.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #5383\n\n### The author should do the following, if applicable\n\n- [x] Add tests\n- [x] Run tests\n- [x] `bun run format:fix && bun run lint:fix` to format the code\n- [ ] Add [TSDoc](https://tsdoc.org/)/[JSDoc](https://jsdoc.app/about-getting-started) to document the code\n\n### What was wrong\n\n`c.req.formData()` keeps only the parsed result and throws the body away. If the body isn't a form, that result is a rejected promise — and it stays in the cache, so every other way of reading the same body gets handed the same rejection:\n\n```ts\napp.post('/', async (c) => {\n  try {\n    await c.req.formData() // JSON body, so this throws\n  } catch {}\n\n  const body = await c.req.json() // throws too\n})\n```\n\n`text()`, `json()`, `arrayBuffer()`, `bytes()` and `blob()` all fail after that.\n\nNode makes it worse than it looks: `raw.formData()` consumes the stream even when it rejects (undici marks the body as used before it checks the media type), so there is nothing left to read afterwards — `raw.text()` throws `Body is unusable`. The bytes have to be read *before* the parse, not after.\n\n### The fix\n\n`c.req.parseBody()` already gets this right: it reads the bytes first and parses them afterwards, so a failed parse leaves the body readable. This makes `formData()` follow the same order, reusing `bufferToFormData()` — which is still the runtime's own parser, just fed from the cached bytes instead of the live stream:\n\n```ts\nif (key === 'formData') {\n  return (bodyCache.formData = this.arrayBuffer().then((buffer) =>\n    bufferToFormData(buffer, raw.headers.get('content-type') ?? '').then((formData) => {\n      // ...\n      return formData\n    })\n  ))\n}\n```\n\n### Keeping `bodyCache` the shape callers expect\n\n`cloneRawRequest()` and the cache middleware both read `Object.keys(bodyCache)[0]` and expect `formData` there once a form has been parsed:\n\n- `src/request.ts` — `cloneRawRequest()`\n- `src/middleware/cache/index.ts`\n\nSo the original order is restored **only when the parse succeeds**. After a failure the raw bytes stay first, which is exactly what makes the other representations readable again. Both of those callers keep working with no changes.\n\n### Tests\n\nAdded to `src/request.test.ts`, next to the existing `should not break body methods after parseBody() with non-form content-type`:\n\n- `text()` / `json()` / `arrayBuffer()` / `bytes()` / `blob()`, each after a failed `formData()`\n- a second `formData()` still reports the parse failure\n- trying another representation after a failed parse (the `try`/`catch` fallback)\n\nSix of the seven fail without the change and pass with it.\n\n- `vitest --run src/request.test.ts src/middleware/cache/index.test.ts src/utils/body.test.ts` — 253 passed\n- full suite — 5141 passed, 44 skipped. The 12 failures in `color` / `logger` / `dev` / `compress(node)` are colour- and TTY-dependent and fail the same way on an unmodified checkout\n- `tsc -p tsconfig.spec.json --noEmit` — clean\n- `bun run format:fix && bun run lint:fix` — no further changes\n\n### Out of scope\n\nAfter a *successful* `formData()`, `text()` still returns the re-serialized form instead of the original bytes. Same root cause, different trigger — fixing it would change the cache shape on the success path too, and with it the two callers above, so it belongs in its own change.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5384/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/5384/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":31457647814,"node_id":"CE_lADOGiE5WM8AAAABRDXQ-88AAAAHUwWcxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/events/3